The cache root is one shared store, safe for concurrent processes, whose large tier (`DIR/v1/artifacts`) is bounded: each run accounts to a partition (`--cache-partition`, `DAFNY_CACHE_PARTITION`, by default one per project directory) with its own budget (`--cache-partition-budget`), an entry is deleted only when no partition holds it, unused partitions expire (`--cache-orphan-days`), and a store-wide cap (`--cache-size-cap`) deletes the least recently used entries. A new `dafny cache` command keeps a partition's entries under a tag (`keep --tag`), releases a tag, enforces the limits (`gc`) and reports the store's contents (`status`).
